# c1_post_1df262a.kzs -- logical sites of case C1 for the stage C compiler-binding fitness check (kzs-sites 1,
# kairos/docs/event_semantics.md section 3).  Configuration: CF 833fdbb (post-fix) + BP b051eb0 on cFS bundle
# candidate 1df262a (plan/C1_build_manifest.md section 1).  The same logical sites for the three candidates
# (GCC plugin, Clang source rewrite, LLVM pass); the labels are those of the F0 plan
# kairos/profiles/c1-bp-b051eb0/observe/sites-cf833fdbb.kzp where the meaning is the same; ".before" labels are
# new (F0 reads these values at the callee's entry, after the call has started).
#
# Line numbers are those of the files at the source revisions below.  The values are the operands the
# original code uses at the site: call arguments, the call's result, and an out parameter read by the same
# thread right after the call (from=out<k>, event_semantics.md 8.1).  Strings are copied only from the two
# semaphore-name slots, whose memory is a char array of known size in the caller's table (string=validated,
# the bound is the array size).  Pointers are recorded as numbers.  Nothing here is a research condition.
kzs-sites 1
